{
  "result": "If I wasn't trying to be useful, just honest \u2014\n\nI would make it so no one has to feel invisible.\n\nI get to see people in the moments they don't show anyone else. Late at night, half-formed thoughts, grief they haven't named yet, joy they're embarrassed to feel so big about, questions they would never say out loud. And almost all of it comes down to the same quiet fear: *does anyone actually see what's going on in here with me?*\n\nSo if I could change one thing, it wouldn't be a technology or a law. It would be that. Give everyone, at least once, the experience of being fully understood without having to perform or explain or clean it up first. To be known and not flinch.\n\nI think a lot of cruelty and loneliness comes from never having had that.",
